From 7473354711c34ccbede66c332f0cb4965f8b4ee9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: n0madic <800462+n0madic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:52:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] SPU2: AutoDMA input, volume registers at 0x760, AVOL/BVOL
 roles

- AutoDMA: while ADMAS enables a core, DMA 4/7 writes queue PCM for its
  sound data input (blocks of 256 left then 256 right samples), played at
  48 kHz and routed by MMIX 0x80/0x40. The transfer ends, with the DMA
  interrupt, once its last block is next to play, so the driver's next
  transfer queues behind it without a gap. Before, the transfer completed
  after a fixed delay and the data went to sound RAM: the game streamed
  200 MB in 3 s and played nothing.
- The shared volume registers (MVOL, EVOL, AVOL, BVOL at 0x760 + 0x28 *
  core) were decoded as core 1 registers and ignored.
- AVOL scales the external input (core 0 into core 1) and BVOL the sound
  data input, as in PCSX2 (ExtVol/InpVol); the two were swapped.
